The signature doesn't pass a buffer length... Let's use a fixed buffer. Is PATH_MAX defined via limits.h on Linux? PATH_MAX is in <linux/limits.h> / <limits.h>. On glibc, PATH_MAX is defined in limits.h (4096). Hmm, to be portable, let's dynamically size: strlen(name) + 128. malloc. Safer. Let's do this:

```c
int open_treefile(char *name, mode_t mode, off_t size, off_t pos, pthread_mutex_t *mutex) {
	int fd;
	size_t pathlen = strlen(name) + (TREE_MAXLEVELS+1) * 11 + 1;
	char *path = malloc(pathlen);
	if (!path) return -1;
	strcpy(path, name);
	off_t ppos;
	pthread_mutex_lock(mutex);
	construct_path(path, pathlen, size, pos, &ppos);
	mkdir_path(path);
	fd = open(path, mode | O_CREAT, 0600);
	pthread_mutex_unlock(mutex);
	free(path);
	return fd;
